  "story": "Guests at a Colorado dog-breeding facility were shocked to discover that authorities had been searching for their 10 missing doberman puppies since August 24th. The puppies, valued at around $15,000 each, were last seen on August 22nd and are still unaccounted for. Paul Peavey, a 57-year-old resident of Idaho Springs, Colorado, was found shot to death on August 24th, days after he had been reported missing. Authorities believe Peavey was killed by Sergio Ferrer, a 36-year-old man who had been considered a person of interest from early on in the investigation. Ferrer admitted to shooting Peavey but claimed it was in self-defense after an argument over illegal activities. A member of the search party, Bruce Boynton, noted that things were not as they should be at the property, and authorities found numerous items belonging to Peavey at Ferrer's home, including a phone, jewelry, and metal detectors. The case is still under investigation, and the district attorney's office will determine the final charges to be filed against Ferrer. "
